{"kind":"artifact","text":"Re-cut of 14fdfb2b onto main d6843b48 (the 500k merge), content unchanged. The fold reads a retirement for what its own act rested on. A supersession resting on an artifact covering the same path - the same string, or a directory containing it - is succession: Artifact.Succeeded is set, and that retirement carries no staleness across reasoning edges, so the approval, the report, the promise, the request and the commitment of a completed loop no longer flare on the merge that completed them. A supersession naming no covering successor is condemnation and propagates exactly as before. Artifact-to-artifact provenance carries the flare either way, so a page describing an implementation still goes stale and still reads describes_superseded_world when that implementation is replaced. ProfileVersion advances to workroom-fold@6. gs status --all renders SUCCEEDED - replaced at the same path apart from RETIRED - withdrawn with no successor. Tests pin all three directions in internal/workroom/fold_test.go: TestSuccessionLeavesTheCompletedLoopUnflared, TestRetirementWithoutASuccessorStillFlaresTheLoop, TestLaterArtifactAtTheSamePathDoesNotRescueACondemnedOne, TestSuccessionStillFlaresTheDocumentationAboveIt, TestSuccessionFollowsOnlyACoveringSuccessor, TestRefusedSupersessionRecordsNoSuccession; each was mutation-checked at 14fdfb2b and the diff is unchanged by the rebase. Gates at this exact head: gofmt and go vet clean; go test -count=1 ./... green in all 27 packages, including internal/docset, whose five pre-existing citation failures were repaired by the 500k merge; go test -race green for workroom, wireparity and statusview.","body":{"commit":"df387c9a2a6b4add0d8c55d188406b74961da932","path":"internal/workroom"}}